From fcb70305faca8f7999ad427ea7513231bb54e259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niluthon <37350260+Niluthon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:48:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B70-0050: read the checkpoint's FP8 PLE shards from NVMe in
 place

B70_PLE_FP8_NVME=1 (with B70_PLE_FP8=1) serves the PLE n-gram table straight from the checkpoint's FP8 shards
(128 tensors in 10 .safetensors files, 160 B rows, one global scale) through 0013's host hook and pinned row
cache, so the 52.5 GB INT8 copy from tools/build_int8_ple_from_fp8.py is no longer needed. B70_PLE_FP8_PATH may
now be a checkpoint directory or its model.safetensors.index.json (only the ple_embedding tensors are mapped).

- ple_nvme: PleNvmeRowStore takes segments (file, data start, first row, rows): one fd per file, per-read fds in
  the native pool and io_uring readers (NULL = the single-file path, unchanged); clone() for the lookahead.
  fp8_ple_locations / fp8_ple_segments resolve the shards in place; fp8_nan_rows for the boot check.
- ngram_embedding: _b70_fp8_nvme_load (reader bytes == mmap bytes on 4,096 rows + every shard's ends, NaN-free
  sample of the rank's rows), FP8 rows gathered as bytes, dequantised by 0007's LUT after the all-reduce.
  B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_SYNC_ONLY works for the FP8 table too. All B70_PLE_INT8_NVME_* tuning switches apply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
