 class PleNvmeRowStore:
-    """Read 164-byte table rows from the file with O_DIRECT (one fd per rank).
-
-    Row g is at ``data_start + row_bytes * g``. Each row is one 4 KiB read,
-    or 8 KiB when it crosses a page boundary. Reads go into page-aligned
-    anonymous-mmap bounce slots (8 KiB each) and are split into contiguous
-    batches over ``io_threads`` workers, each looping ``os.preadv`` (which
-    releases the GIL). A failed or short read is retried 3 times (1/10/100
-    ms), then raises; nothing is ever zero-filled.
+    """Read fixed-size table rows from the file(s) with O_DIRECT.
+
+    Row g is at ``data_start + row_bytes * g`` of ``path``. Each row is one
+    4 KiB read, or 8 KiB when it crosses a page boundary. Reads go into
+    page-aligned anonymous-mmap bounce slots (8 KiB each) and are split into
+    contiguous batches over ``io_threads`` workers, each looping
+    ``os.preadv`` (which releases the GIL). A failed or short read is retried
+    3 times (1/10/100 ms), then raises; nothing is ever zero-filled.
+
+    ``segments`` (0050): the table is split over several files, e.g. the
+    checkpoint's FP8 PLE shards (128 tensors in 10 .safetensors files, data
+    at arbitrary, unaligned offsets). A list of ``(path, data_start,
+    first_row, rows)`` covering [0, num_rows) without gaps, in row order;
+    row g of segment s is at ``data_start + row_bytes * (g - first_row)`` of
+    its file. Each distinct file is opened once. ``path`` / ``data_start``
+    are then those of the first segment and only kept for logging.
 
     ``reader`` (0013b): "py" is the above; "native" replaces the Python
     workers by a C pthread pool (``io_threads`` threads, one ctypes call per
@@ -596,27 +616,67 @@ class PleNvmeRowStore:
